"""orch-sweep — M-218 P2 (quota ledger and worker rotation), M-284 (dead/stale
wakeups, partial stops, stuck queues), M-268 (committee stuck-list)

One deterministic pass over the live board for the Orchestrator tick.
Run by the tick as a SINGLE tool call; all internal multica/gh calls are the
script's own subprocesses, they do not count against the tick's tool-call
budget (tick contract: at most 6 tool calls plus one per action).

Read-only by default. `--apply-cooldown` additionally writes confirmed quota
cooldowns to M-86 metadata key `quota_ledger`. It never touches card status,
assignments, comments or PRs — acting on the output stays the agent's job.

`--stuck-list` prints only the compact committee slice:
  {at, tool:"orch-sweep", mode:"stuck-list", hash, triggers, items}
Triggers (deterministic, no LLM judgment):
  (a) green PR with no verdict on its SHA for >30 min, on a card with no
      live run and no pending wakeup (verdict-amendment M-268);
  (b) card idle >2 h with a resume already tried
      (`orch_baseline.resume.<card>.count>=1`);
  (c) card `blocked` >4 h;
  (d) >=3 cards share one `failure_class`/`reason` code.
Items are {card, trigger, age_min, pr} — small enough to keep M-86 metadata
(`stuck_list` + ledger + baseline) under the 4 KB cap.

Output: one JSON object on stdout:
  { at, board[], gate_waiting[], todo_reroutes[], ledger{}, counts{},
    wip_breaches[], eligible{engineers[],reviewers[]}, stuck{} }

Only confirmed quota signals cool a shared account (leader scope 2026-11-07):
  * OMP Go      `429 Go usage limit exceeded retry-after-ms=...` / GoUsageLimitError
  * Claude      `You've hit your weekly limit|session limit · resets <time>`
  * Codex       `usage limit` (generic form)
  * Pi upstream `429 {"type":"rate_limit_error", ...}`        (short cooldown)
Unknown / generic errors (Codebuddy "error result without details", Freebuff
generic, 401 config errors, idle watchdog) NEVER cool an account: they become
`unknown` or plain failure classes and go to triage.

There is no remaining-quota field in `multica runtime usage` — the ledger is
observed-signal only; do not invent one.
"""

